-- title:
--   Local quotient form of a pulled-back section on Ω_C
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic base.** Fix a prime $r$ and a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), together with an irreducible element $\pi$, such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has cardinality $r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$; let $K_0$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified coefficients.** Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, and $\mathrm{Fr}$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism of it, subject to: $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo it (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of positive degree has a root modulo it (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo it for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Valuation of the determinant.** Let $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a group homomorphism such that $v\!\det(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Group data.** Let $G$ be a group, $\sigma:G\to\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma\le G$ a subgroup such that some $z\in\Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix with $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ (`hcent`) and some $w\in\Gamma$ has $v\!\det(\sigma w)=1$ (`hodd`); let $\Gamma'\le G$ consist exactly of the $x\in\Gamma$ with $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ even (`hΓ'`). Let $\rho:G\to\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ be the homomorphism induced by $\sigma$ (`hρ`). The image $\rho(\Gamma')$ is assumed to have finite stabiliser at every vertex of the lattice tree of $(\mathcal O,K_0)$ (`hdisc`) and to have finitely many orbit representatives among the vertices: there is a finite set $S$ of vertices such that every vertex has a translate in $S$ (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The quotient.** Let $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be a proper flat morphism of schemes, and let $\Theta$ assign, to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra map and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (an object of the functor `Omega K₀ π`: a family of lines in the base changes of the full lattices of $K_0^2$, with invertible quotients, monotone under inclusions, equivariant for scalars, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$) to the $B$-points of $f$, that is, the morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. Four hypotheses describe $\Theta$: naturality in $B$ (`hΘnat`); invariance under the twisted $\Gamma$-action (`hΘinv`), where `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $g$ relates $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi',P')$ when $\psi'=\psi\circ\mathrm{Fr}^{-v\det(g)}$ and $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $g^{-1}$; the fibre description (`hΘfib`): for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent and every $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$, the map $P\mapsto\Theta_k(\psi,P)$ is onto the $k$-points of $f$ and identifies two data precisely when they are related by the twisted action of some $\gamma\in\Gamma$; and the universal property (`hΘuniv`): for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and every natural, $\Gamma$-invariant family $\rho'$ of maps into the nilpotent points of $T$ there is a natural family $u$ from the nilpotent points of $f$ to those of $T$ with $u\circ\Theta=\rho'$, and any natural $u'$ with $u'\circ\Theta=\rho'$ agrees with $u$.
--
--   **Analytic frame.** Let $C$ be an algebraically closed $K_0$-algebra field carrying a valuation $v$ with values in $\Gamma_0$, complete for it, let $R$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with a map to $C$, compatibly with $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$, let $\varpi$ be a pseudo-uniformiser of $K_0$ in $C$ (an element of $K_0$ whose valuation in $C$ lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and whose powers bound the valuation of every nonzero element of $K_0$ from both sides), and let `hF : IsAdicFrame π ϖ R` hold, i.e. $\pi$ is irreducible, $R\to C$ is injective with image the set of elements of valuation $\le 1$, $R$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, the elements of $K_0$ of valuation $\le1$ in $C$ are exactly those of $\mathcal O$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and $\pi$ and $\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Let $\psi_0:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to R$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map. Further: the valuation has rank one in the sense that for $v(x)<1$ and $y\ne0$ some power $v(x)^n\le v(y)$ (`hrk`); the value group is cofinal downwards, i.e. every $\varepsilon\ne0$ bounds the valuation of some nonzero $y$ (`hval`); $\varpi$ is exhausting, i.e. every point of the Drinfeld upper half-plane $\Omega_C=C\setminus K_0$ lies in some affinoid $\Omega_n$ (`hex`); and the ring of functions on $\Omega_C$ holomorphic on every $\Omega_n$ is a domain.
--
--   **Uniformisation.** Let $\Phi$ send each adic point $x$ (a compatible system of Deligne data over the quotients $R/(\pi^{n+1})$) to an $R$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, subject to the four clauses of `hΦ`: for every $x$ and $n$, the reduction of $\Phi x$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ equals $\Theta$ applied to the pair consisting of $\psi_0$ reduced modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ and the $n$-th datum of $x$; $\Phi$ is surjective; $\Phi x=\Phi x'$ if and only if $x'=x\cdot\sigma\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma'$; and the passage from $R$-points to $C$-points is injective, every $C$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ arising this way.
--
--   **Base change.** Let $s_C:\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be the morphism induced by $\mathcal O\to K_0\to C$ (`hsC`), and assume the pullback $\mathcal X_C$ of $f$ along $s_C$ is an integral scheme.
--
--   **Three further hypotheses.** `hclear` (pointwise algebraic clearing): for every open $U\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ containing the generic point, every $s\in\mathcal O(U)$, every adic point $x$ and every $C$-point $q$ of $\mathcal X_C$ whose first projection is $\Phi x$ composed with $\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}R$ and whose second projection is the identity, there exist an open $V\subseteq\mathcal X$ through which $\Phi x$ factors, an open $W\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ with $W$ inside the preimage of $V$, through which $q$ factors and which contains the generic point, integers $m,m'$, sections $\mathrm{num}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\mathcal O(V)$ and $\mathrm{den}:\mathrm{Fin}\,m'\to\mathcal O(V)$ and constants $c_{\mathrm{num}},c_{\mathrm{den}}$ in $C$ such that, writing $D=\sum_j c_{\mathrm{den},j}\,\mathrm{den}_j$ and $N=\sum_i c_{\mathrm{num},i}\,\mathrm{num}_i$ for the corresponding combinations on $W$ (constants pulled back along the second projection, sections along the first): $D\neq0$ in $\mathcal O(W)$; $s\cdot D=N$ on $W\sqcap U$; and if $q$ factors through $U$ then $D$ is a unit on some smaller open $W'\le W$ through which $q$ still factors.
--
--   `htube` (tubewise holomorphy): for every $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, every open $V\subseteq\mathcal X$ and every $p\in\mathcal O(V)$ there are $m\in\mathbb N$ and finite sets $L_k,M_k\subseteq C\times C$ $(k<m)$ whose pairs all have nonzero second coordinate, such that, with $E_g$ the edge region $\mathrm{vertexTube}(g)\cup\mathrm{edgeTube}(g)\cup\mathrm{vertexTube}(g\cdot\mathrm{edgeFlip})$ and $E_{g,k}$ the subset of $E_g$ cut out by $v(\varrho)\le v(\mu_{g}^{-1}(z)-e)$ for $(e,\varrho)\in L_k$ and $v(\mu_g^{-1}(z)-e)\le v(\varrho)$ for $(e,\varrho)\in M_k$ (here $\mu_g^{-1}$ is the Möbius action of the class of $g^{-1}$ in $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$): every coordinate $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ of an adic point $x$ which lies in $E_g$ and for which $\Phi x$ factors through $V$ lies in some $E_{g,k}$; conversely, for each $k$, an adic point whose coordinate lies in $E_{g,k}$ has $\Phi x$ factoring through $V$; and for each $k$ there is a function $F$ on $E_{g,k}$ lying in `holOn C` (a uniform limit of uniformly bounded pole-free rational functions) whose value at the coordinate of any adic point $x$ with $\Phi x$ factoring through $V$ is the image in $C$ of the value of $p$ at $\Phi x$.
--
--   `hfin` (affinoid finiteness of exceptional coordinates): for every open $U\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ containing the generic point and every $n$, the set of points of the affinoid $\Omega_n$ which are coordinates of adic points $x$ admitting a $C$-point $q$ of $\mathcal X_C$, with projections as above, that does not factor through $U$, is finite.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every open $U\subseteq\mathcal X_C$ containing the generic point, every section $s\in\mathcal O(U)$ and every function $F:\Omega_C\to C$ on the upper half-plane $\Omega_C=C\setminus K_0$, if $F$ interpolates $s$ in the sense that for every adic point $x$, every $z\in\Omega_C$ with $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$, and every $C$-point $q$ of $\mathcal X_C$ whose first projection is $\Phi x$ composed with $\operatorname{Spec}C\to\operatorname{Spec}R$, whose second projection is the identity, and which factors through $U$, the value $F(z)$ equals the value of $s$ at $q$ (the element of $C$ obtained from $(q^\ast s)$ by restriction to the whole of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec}C)\cong C$), then: for every adic point $x$, every $z\in\Omega_C$ with $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$ and every such $C$-point $q$ factoring through $U$, there exist $N\in\mathbb N$ such that the closed disc $D=\{w\in C: v(w-z)\le v(\varpi)^{N}\}$ is contained in $\Omega_C$, and functions $a,b:D\to C$, both lying in `holOn C D`, with $b$ nonvanishing at the centre (that is, $b(w)\ne0$ for $w\in D$ with $w=z$), such that $b(w)\,F(w)=a(w)$ for all $w\in D$.
--
--   This is the local, disc-wise form of the statement that a section of the structure sheaf of the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient $\mathcal X_C$, interpolated along the $p$-adic uniformisation $\Phi$, pulls back to a function on the Drinfeld upper half-plane that is meromorphic near every coordinate of an adic point over the open where the section is defined: near such a point it is a quotient of two rigid-holomorphic functions on a closed disc, with nonvanishing denominator at the centre. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_invariant_chartwiseMeromorphic_pullback_of_cover_clearing_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_invariant_chartwiseMeromorphic_pullback_of_cover_clearing_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient) to produce the $\Gamma'$-invariant chartwise meromorphic pullback.
